<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- ============================================================================
    Slim accent scrollbar (2026-07-14, fixed 2026-07-15) - replaces FluentTheme's default
    ScrollBar/ScrollViewer look app-wide (this file has no per-module prefix on purpose - it
    targets the bare `ScrollBar` type selector, not a Class, so every ScrollViewer/ListBox/TextBox
    in the app picks it up with zero per-view changes). Four separate problems with the stock
    look, all traced against the real Avalonia 12.0.5 source
    (src/Avalonia.Themes.Fluent/Controls/ScrollBar.xaml and ScrollViewer.xaml) rather than guessed:

    1. It overlaps content. ScrollViewer's default ControlTemplate lays out content in a
       Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" (content | scrollbar), but its `^[AllowAutoHide=True]`
       style (AllowAutoHide defaults to True) makes the content presenter span BOTH columns/rows,
       so the scrollbar's own column sits visually on top of the tail end of the content instead
       of reserving its own space. Fixed below by forcing AllowAutoHide="False" app-wide - content
       always stays in column/row 0, the scrollbar's Auto column/row is genuinely reserved, never
       overlaid.
    2. It's the plain gray Win32-style bar, and FluentTheme's own thumb additionally "expands" on
       hover via a RenderTransform scale reset (see `^[IsExpanded=true]` in the real ScrollBar.xaml)
       - which would fight a fixed slim width anyway. Rather than fight that per-state animation,
       ScrollBar's whole Template is replaced below with a plain fixed-width Track (no expand
       state, no page-arrow buttons - modern slim scrollbars don't need click-arrows, matches the
       already-established "own the whole template" approach from FlatButtonTemplate/
       SCSkinListItemTemplate/CCTextBoxTemplate for the same reason: FluentTheme's per-state
       Setters target template-internal parts and can't be reliably overridden piecemeal).
    3. (Found 2026-07-15, reported as "accent color applies inconsistently / animation resets at
       random moments / everywhere else just plain gray with no animation".) The first pass at #2
       only overrode ScrollBar's `Template` via a plain external `<Style Selector="ScrollBar:...">`
       Setter, but never replaced ScrollBar's whole `Theme` - so FluentTheme's own implicit
       ControlTheme (`x:Key="{x:Type ScrollBar}"`, still the active Theme for every ScrollBar since
       nothing overrode it) stayed fully active underneath, INCLUDING its own nested
       `^[IsExpanded=true] -> ^ /template/ Thumb` style, which sets Background to FluentTheme's own
       neutral ScrollBarThumbBackgroundColor and resets RenderTransform to "none" whenever the
       ScrollBar's IsExpanded pseudo-class flips true (which Avalonia sets internally on hover,
       unrelated to which Template is in effect). `/template/ Thumb` walks whatever template is
       ACTUALLY in use for that instance - including our own SlimVerticalScrollBarTemplate's Thumb
       - so FluentTheme's own ControlTheme kept clobbering our Thumb's Background every time the
       user hovered, fighting our SlimScrollThumbTheme's :pointerover/:pressed Setters and our
       BrushTransition in a way that looked "random" (tied to hover/IsExpanded timing, not any
       specific view). Fixed by replacing the ENTIRE `{x:Type ScrollBar}` ControlTheme below
       (matching FluentTheme's own resource key so ours wins the lookup, not just patching
       Template) - no `[IsExpanded=true]` style exists in ours at all, so nothing is left to
       compete with SlimScrollThumbTheme's own state Setters.
    4. (Found 2026-07-15, reported as the skins list's scrollbar sitting on top of a card's right
       edge, screenshot at Fuckups/Scroll_over_content.png - the exact "overlap" point 1 above was
       meant to fix, but only for that ONE control.) Point 1's `<Style Selector="ScrollViewer">`
       Setter never reaches a ListBox's own internal scroll area: FluentTheme's real
       `x:Key="{x:Type ListBox}"` template hosts `ScrollViewer Name="PART_ScrollViewer"` with
       `AllowAutoHide="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.AllowAutoHide)}"` - a TemplateBinding to the
       ATTACHED property as set on the ListBox itself, not a local default. First attempt: set that
       attached property broadly (`<Style Selector="Control"><Setter Property=
       "ScrollViewer.AllowAutoHide".../></Style>` below) so the TemplateBinding would forward it -
       theoretically sound (confirmed FluentTheme's own ListBox ControlTheme sets other
       ScrollViewer.* attached properties the exact same way) but did NOT fix the bug on rebuild/
       retest, for a reason not fully pinned down (possibly a style-application-timing gap between
       when the attached property resolves on the ListBox and when its own Template's
       TemplateBinding first reads it). Rather than keep chasing that indirection, applied this
       project's own established fallback for exactly this situation (see point 2's own reasoning,
       and CCTextBoxTemplate/FlatButtonTemplate/SCSkinListItemTemplate elsewhere): own the WHOLE
       `{x:Type ListBox}` ControlTheme too, hardcoding `AllowAutoHide="False"` as a literal value
       directly on `PART_ScrollViewer` instead of forwarding it through any binding at all - removes
       the indirection instead of trying to win it. The attached-property Style below is left in
       place as a harmless no-op / defense in depth for any other TemplateBinding-forwarding control
       (ComboBox, multi-line TextBox) that might need the same treatment later.

    Thumb color tiers (AccentScrollThumbBrush/AccentScrollThumbHoverBrush) live in
    AccentColors.axaml alongside the app's other accent tiers, not as local literals here - same
    "single source of truth per theme" reasoning as everywhere else, and it's what makes this
    scrollbar re-tint correctly on light/dark switch for free.
    ============================================================================ -->

    <Styles.Resources>
        <!-- Own ControlTheme (not just a ControlTemplate) so the thumb's :pointerover/:pressed
        states can each carry their own Background - same pattern as FluentTheme's own
        FluentScrollBarThumb, just re-pointed at this app's accent tokens instead of FluentTheme's
        neutral ScrollBarThumbFill* resources. Pressed reuses the fully-opaque AccentPrimaryBrush
        directly rather than a third baked-alpha tier - see AccentColors.axaml's own comment. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="SlimScrollThumbTheme" TargetType="Thumb">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AccentScrollThumbBrush}"/>
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                        <Border.Transitions>
                            <Transitions>
                                <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="0:0:0.15"/>
                            </Transitions>
                        </Border.Transitions>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AccentScrollThumbHoverBrush}"/>
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pressed">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AccentPrimaryBrush}"/>
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <!-- Invisible click-to-page hit areas either side of the thumb - functional (clicking the
        track still pages the scroll position) but undecorated, same as FluentTheme's own
        FluentScrollBarPageButton. -->
        <ControlTemplate x:Key="SlimScrollPageButtonTemplate" TargetType="RepeatButton">
            <Border Background="Transparent"/>
        </ControlTemplate>

        <ControlTemplate x:Key="SlimVerticalScrollBarTemplate" TargetType="ScrollBar">
            <Track Minimum="{TemplateBinding Minimum}"
                   Maximum="{TemplateBinding Maximum}"
                   Value="{TemplateBinding Value, Mode=TwoWay}"
                   ViewportSize="{TemplateBinding ViewportSize}"
                   Orientation="Vertical"
                   IsDirectionReversed="True">
                <Track.DecreaseButton>
                    <RepeatButton Template="{StaticResource SlimScrollPageButtonTemplate}" Focusable="False"/>
                </Track.DecreaseButton>
                <Track.IncreaseButton>
                    <RepeatButton Template="{StaticResource SlimScrollPageButtonTemplate}" Focusable="False"/>
                </Track.IncreaseButton>
                <Thumb Theme="{StaticResource SlimScrollThumbTheme}"
                       Width="6" MinHeight="24" CornerRadius="3"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"/>
            </Track>
        </ControlTemplate>

        <ControlTemplate x:Key="SlimHorizontalScrollBarTemplate" TargetType="ScrollBar">
            <Track Minimum="{TemplateBinding Minimum}"
                   Maximum="{TemplateBinding Maximum}"
                   Value="{TemplateBinding Value, Mode=TwoWay}"
                   ViewportSize="{TemplateBinding ViewportSize}"
                   Orientation="Horizontal">
                <Track.DecreaseButton>
                    <RepeatButton Template="{StaticResource SlimScrollPageButtonTemplate}" Focusable="False"/>
                </Track.DecreaseButton>
                <Track.IncreaseButton>
                    <RepeatButton Template="{StaticResource SlimScrollPageButtonTemplate}" Focusable="False"/>
                </Track.IncreaseButton>
                <Thumb Theme="{StaticResource SlimScrollThumbTheme}"
                       Height="6" MinWidth="24" CornerRadius="3"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
            </Track>
        </ControlTemplate>

        <!-- Replaces FluentTheme's own x:Key="{x:Type ScrollBar}" ControlTheme outright (same key,
        so ours wins the resource lookup) instead of patching individual properties via an external
        Style - see point 3 above. Mirrors FluentTheme's own ^:vertical/^:horizontal nested-Template
        pattern, but deliberately has no [IsExpanded=true] style at all: that's the one FluentTheme
        relies on to "expand" its own default thumb on hover, and it's exactly what was fighting our
        thumb colors. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ScrollBar}" TargetType="ScrollBar">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
            <!-- 10px reserved column/row - a 6px thumb with 2px breathing room either side,
            "narrow" per the brief without being fiddly to grab. -->
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="10"/>
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="10"/>

            <Style Selector="^:vertical">
                <Setter Property="Template" Value="{StaticResource SlimVerticalScrollBarTemplate}"/>
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:horizontal">
                <Setter Property="Template" Value="{StaticResource SlimHorizontalScrollBarTemplate}"/>
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <!-- Replaces FluentTheme's own x:Key="{x:Type ListBox}" ControlTheme outright - see point 4
        above. Identical to the real one (src/Avalonia.Themes.Fluent/Controls/ListBox.xaml, 12.0.5)
        except AllowAutoHide is a literal "False" on PART_ScrollViewer instead of
        "{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.AllowAutoHide)}" - no attached-property forwarding left to
        get wrong. Only ListBox.SCSkinsList (Skin Changer) uses ListBox anywhere in this app today,
        but this lives here rather than SkinChangerStyles.axaml so any future ListBox usage gets the
        fix for free, matching this file's own "zero per-view opt-in" design. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ListBox}" TargetType="ListBox">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource SystemControlForegroundBaseHighBrush}" />
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource SystemControlBackgroundChromeMediumLowBrush}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource SystemControlForegroundBaseHighBrush}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="{DynamicResource ListBoxBorderThemeThickness}" />
            <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility" Value="Disabled" />
            <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility" Value="Auto" />
            <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.IsScrollChainingEnabled" Value="True" />
            <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.IsScrollInertiaEnabled" Value="True" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border Name="border"
                            ClipToBounds="{TemplateBinding ClipToBounds}"
                            Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                            CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                        <ScrollViewer Name="PART_ScrollViewer"
                                      AllowAutoHide="False"
                                      VerticalSnapPointsType="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.VerticalSnapPointsType)}"
                                      HorizontalSnapPointsType="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.HorizontalSnapPointsType)}"
                                      HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility)}"
                                      VerticalScrollBarVisibility="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility)}"
                                      IsScrollChainingEnabled="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.IsScrollChainingEnabled)}"
                                      IsScrollInertiaEnabled="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.IsScrollInertiaEnabled)}"
                                      IsDeferredScrollingEnabled="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.IsDeferredScrollingEnabled)}"
                                      BringIntoViewOnFocusChange="{TemplateBinding (ScrollViewer.BringIntoViewOnFocusChange)}">
                            <ItemsPresenter Name="PART_ItemsPresenter"
                                            ItemsPanel="{TemplateBinding ItemsPanel}"
                                            Margin="{TemplateBinding Padding}"/>
                        </ScrollViewer>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
        </ControlTheme>
    </Styles.Resources>

    <!-- Reserve space instead of overlaying - see point 1 above. Covers bare ScrollViewer
    instances used standalone (e.g. the Skin Changer's Screenshots panel). -->
    <Style Selector="ScrollViewer">
        <Setter Property="AllowAutoHide" Value="False"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- Covers ScrollViewer instances hosted INSIDE another control's own template (ListBox,
    ComboBox, multi-line TextBox, ...) - see point 4 above. Those forward AllowAutoHide via
    TemplateBinding to this attached property as set on the host control itself, which outranks
    the plain ScrollViewer Style above regardless of selector specificity. Applied broadly to
    Control rather than enumerating every host type - harmless no-op on anything that never reads
    it via TemplateBinding, matches this file's existing "global override, zero per-view opt-in"
    approach. -->
    <Style Selector="Control">
        <Setter Property="ScrollViewer.AllowAutoHide" Value="False"/>
    </Style>

</Styles>
